; S65sw58 (SGOLD) Bluetooth PAN MTU 1500 for bt-pan_SG: L2CAP limit 1696, BNEP MTU 1691.
; EXPERIMENTAL, untested on the phone. Apply only to S65v58. Generated by port-mtu-s65.py.
;
; Same idea as bt-pan-mtu.vkp (EL71): stock RX/TX ACL pool counts, bigger objects, all
; 0x14F..0x158 limits on the RX/TX data path raised. Not ported from EL71: the JSApi ring and
; the Java hooks (bt-pan does not use Java), HCI Host Buffer Size (stays stock).
; Affects every BT profile; Java L2CAP apps can now negotiate MTU above 335.
; The stub uses A0D9FF00..A0D9FF0F; check that no other installed patch writes there.

; BT_RX_ACL_HEAP object_size: 0x1B4 -> 0x704, count stays 0x1A (descriptor A0096080).
; Backing = count * align4(size + 0xF), taken from the heap at boot:
;   26 * 0x1C0 = 0x2D80 -> 26 * 0x710 = 0xB7A0 (+0x8A20)
0x0009608C: B4010000 04070000

; BT_TX_ACL_HEAP object_size: 0x174 -> 0x704, count stays 0x24 (descriptor A0096054).
;   36 * 0x180 = 0x3600 -> 36 * 0x710 = 0xFE40 (+0xC840). RX+TX: +0x15260 (84.6 KiB RAM)
0x00096060: 74010000 04070000

; RX ACL block request (A0B3F996): 0x1A0 -> 0x6F0. Data starts 48 bytes into the block,
; so an RX block now holds 0x6C0 bytes (L2CAP SDU 0x6A0 + header, reassembled in place).
0x00B3F9B6: FF21A131 DE21C900

; TX ACL block request (A0B3FA14): 0x160 -> 0x6F0. BTLP copies a whole SDU to +0x10.
0x00B3FA48: FF216131 DE21C900

; Transport callback GetDataSizeRxAcl (+0x70 of the adapter table): 0x158 -> 0x6A8
; (the same getter as EL71 A08BB3AE).
0x00B34226: FF205930 D520C000

; Incoming HCI ACL payload limit (A0B7E9BA): 0x14F -> 0x6A0.
0x00B7E9C6: FF225032 D422D200

; BTLSAR continuation append limit (A0B7E49E): 0x154 -> 0x6A0. The other check right after
; it compares with the SDU length from the L2CAP header, as stock.
0x00B7E560: FF255535 D425ED00

; LDAEstReq (A0B3E282) outgoing connection: rx/tx MTU 48..0x14F -> 48..0x6A0.
0x00B3E2BC: FF275037 D427FF00

; Server registration (A0B3E4FA): the same MTU check, 0x14F -> 0x6A0.
0x00B3E55A: FF275037 D427FF00

; BTLP_uiSendDataOverBT (A0B441C6) chunk: 0x14F -> 0x6A0. Stock splits a longer SDU into
; several L2CAP SDUs; now one SDU per call. A0B7E404 then fragments it into 0x153-byte
; ACL packets (PB=2 + PB=1), an existing path that stock MTUs never reach.
0x00B44204: FF265036 D426F600

; Accept HCI PB=0 (Linux non-flushable start) as a first fragment, like EL71: BTLSAR takes
; only PB=2. BL to the stub, which maps PB=0 to 2 and redoes the cmp and the ldr.
0x00B7E4D6: 02295448 21F213FD

; Thumb stub: cmp r1,#0; bne; movs r1,#2; cmp r1,#2; ldr r0,=0xA86DC518; bx lr
0x00D9FF00: FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF 002900D1022102290048704718C56DA8
